==Background==
==Roles==
* The Rt. Hon. Sir Joseph Porter, [[Order of the Bath|KCB]], [[First Lord of the Admiralty]] (comic [[baritone]])
* Captain Corcoran, Commander of H.M.S. ''Pinafore'' (lyric [[baritone]])
* Ralph{{refn|The traditional British pronunciation of this name is "rafe" ({{IPAc-en|r|eɪ|f}}). Gilbert rhymes it with "waif" in the lyrics of Little Buttercup's Act II song, "A many years ago".|group= n}} Rackstraw, [[Able seaman (rank)|Able Seaman]] ([[tenor]])
* Dick Deadeye, Able Seaman ([[bass-baritone]])
* Bill Bobstay, [[Boatswain]]'s Mate ([[baritone]])
* Bob Becket, Carpenter's Mate ([[bass (voice type)|bass]])
* Josephine, The Captain's Daughter ([[soprano]])
* Cousin Hebe, Sir Joseph's First Cousin ([[mezzo-soprano]])
* Mrs. Cripps (Little Buttercup), A Portsmouth [[Bumboat]] Woman ([[contralto]])
* Chorus of First Lord's Sisters, His Cousins, His Aunts, Sailors, Marines, etc.

